Dear Deans and Directors,

This message is confidential. Please do not forward it beyond your own
budget managers.

The second-quarter reforecast was presented to the Finance and Audit
Committee on 19 February. I want you to hear the position from me
directly, and to know what we are doing about it.

Where we stand

We now expect to finish the fiscal year with an operating surplus of
$1.9 million, against the $4.7 million in the approved budget. The gap
of $2.8 million has three causes:

- The halls on the Brackenridge Campus are 91% full, not the 96% we
  budgeted. That costs us about $0.8 million in residence and dining
  income.
- Several research projects started later than planned, which moves
  about $1.4 million of grant income into next year.
- Energy has cost about $0.6 million more than budgeted.

Tuition income is on budget. Enrolment is in line with the 6,400 we
assumed.

What changes on 1 March

The following controls apply from 1 March 2026 until 30 June 2026.

1. Recruitment to professional and support posts is paused. A vacancy
   may be filled only with the President's written approval. Academic
   posts and posts paid entirely from external grants are not affected.

2. The Institute-wide staff travel budget is reduced by 15%, from
   $2.4 million to $2.04 million. Trips already approved will go ahead.
   New trips will be approved only where the traveller is presenting,
   examining or recruiting students.

3. Any purchase above $20,000 from a non-research budget needs my
   approval before the order is placed, whatever your normal authority.
   Purchases from research grants continue to follow the research
   approval policy.

4. No contingency will be released except for health, safety or legal
   obligations.

If you believe a specific post or purchase should be exempt, send the
Budget Office a one-page case by 13 March. I will reply within five
working days.

What does not change

The cost-of-living adjustment paid in January stands. Annual increments
will be paid on the normal review dates. Scholarships, student support
and the capital programme are untouched.

I will hold a briefing for budget holders on 3 March at 10:00 in the
Vasterling Building, room 2.20. Please come or send a deputy.

Thank you for your help in bringing the year in on plan.

Rufus

Rufus Delacroix-Nwosu
